course: dictionary
lesson: 6353
title: Mow: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word mow can mean to cut grass short, as in «Gardens need regular weeding, mowing and watering». The clues are the words around it: gardens, grass and lawns all point to cutting grass.
explain: The second meaning is used in news reports about war or accidents. «Mow down» means to knock down or kill many people or things quickly. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, a garden or a crash, and that tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «to cut it short» fit «mow the lawn»? Yes. Does it fit a report about people being knocked down? No, so that sentence must mean the other thing.
fact: Mow means to cut grass short, using a lawnmower or a long blade.
fact: «Mow down» means to knock down or kill many people or things quickly.
fact: The verb changes its form: mow, mows, mowed, mowed or mown, mowing.
fact: «Freshly mown grass» means grass that has just been cut.
fact: Keep well away from a running lawnmower, because its blades are very sharp and can throw stones.
exercise: «Gardens need regular weeding, mowing and watering or they quickly grow wild.» What does mowing mean here? | *Cutting the grass short | Painting the garden fence | Pulling up flowers by the roots | Splashing water on the path
exercise: A news report said the crowd was «mown down» by a speeding car. What does mown down mean? | Cut short with a lawnmower | Left to grow wild | *Knocked down or killed quickly | Dried for animals to eat
exercise: «In farming, hay is mown and dried for animals.» What does mown mean in this sentence? | Hidden under a blanket | Watered every day | Sold in a shop | *Cut down with a blade or machine
test: Which of these is a correct past form of mow? | *Mowed | Mows | Mowing | Mowerd
test: «Stay well away from a lawnmower, even when it is off.» Why? | *Its blades are very sharp and can throw stones | Lawnmowers are too heavy to lift | Lawnmowers make the grass grow faster | Lawnmowers only work in the rain
exam: Green sea turtles eat seagrass, and their grazing is «like mowing a lawn»; what does mowing mean there? | *Cutting seagrass short by eating it, which keeps the meadow healthy | Turning green in the sun | Hiding in the sand from predators | Swimming fast through the sea
